r a second language to configure your  website  here we have the information about the  english part for example  the language code where it's located the  content  and the title note that the abbreviation  of the languages are pretty financed so  if you want a portuguese website for  example you need to check  which is the correct abbreviation then  in each language will need their own  menustone5 and a subfolder  within the content folder finally choose  the default  a language that the visitors will see  when visit your  page and for make it visible that the  website is multilingual  check in paramster that show language  is true when you are done with your  edits and you are happy  with your website it's time to put it  online  one way to do this is using netlife  one of the advantages of deploying your  website through nedliver is that  allows you to have a static site for  free and easily  basically it connects to the remote  repository on github to deploy  every change that it makes on the  website it will be automatically  updated after to push to github  it's important that the hugo version  that you are  running locally might match with the  version that the  that netlifer is going to use to build  your site and how to do that  check the first the your local version  of hugo and pick up the nucleophile tomb  to your project raw directory and  specify the hugo version  then in go to the netlife webpage  and login within with with github  to select the repo you've been working  with block down  you will see something like this but  with your information  go to show advanced and just just in  case  write the hugo version and finally you  will have your  website in the latest version of  lockdown  you can set up the hugo version by  running this code  until tonightly file the hugo version  with this function if you want  more information here are some blogs  that i use in this presentation  and you can find me on my website and on  twitter  thank you  [Music] 